coal 41
pump 10
pump 20


! number to pressure test

! we want to load number 3 into steam and back from steam

! it should be easier to load a number from steam first
pump 20
high_pressure_switch 300
release_valve 1
low_pressure_switch 132 ! why we have this numnber is explained below.
release_valve 0 ! -0.1bar

! this algoritm works for all numbers > 0.
set_put 0
press ! 0.5bar, only once

set_put 1
press ! 0.5bar, per itter

set_add
press ! 1bar, per itter

move_belt -4 ! 4bar, per itter

pull 

! looking at the repeating costs and constant costs we can establish a conversion function:
! s(n) = 5.5*n-3.4  we need to add 0.1 on top for rounding error prevention at "press"
! considering a boiler pressure limit of 150 bar, the max. number we can convert at a time is 27.



! now we will try to convert a number into steam. 
! we will need the previous conversion function. 



high_pressure_switch 133
low_pressure_switch 133
set_container 0
release_valve 22 !taking half per tick because move costs 1
move_belt -1



